FINDINGS:

1. [MAJOR] tests/bootstrap_selfhost_test.rs:2187 — The phase's actual new behaviour is that `intern_hash` selects one of 256 buckets, but no test pins distribution. `edge_engineered_collision` only proves a collision resolves; it never asserts that two ordinary names land in *different* buckets. The self-test even prints `collision_bucket` (bootstrap/compiler.rb:2819) and the Rust test never reads it. A degenerate `intern_hash` that returns a constant (every name in bucket 0) would satisfy every assertion here: `repeat_growth`/`other_growth`, `empty_*`, `long_*`, `collision_found`, distinct indexes, the byte-identical fixture, and the type-error test all depend only on dedup correctness, not on which bucket a name selects. So the exact performance regression this phase exists to prevent — falling back to an O(n) scan — cannot be detected by the suite. Fix: have `--intern-selftest` print the number of distinct non-empty buckets (and/or max chain length) after interning a few hundred names, and assert a lower bound; add an assertion that two ordinary names hash to different buckets.
   - This is verified by inspection of the assertions and the selftest output keys; I did not run the suite.

2. [MINOR] bootstrap/compiler.rb:2737 — `intern_bucket_add` rebuilds the entire 256-entry bucket array (and allocates a fresh 256-element list) for every newly seen name, so insertion remains O(INTERN_BUCKETS) per distinct name. The change only improves lookups. This is acceptable at 256 but is the cost the phase neither tests nor documents as a trade-off; combined with finding 1, an insertion regression is invisible.

3. [MINOR] bootstrap/compiler.rb:2756 — ~90 lines of test-only `intern_selftest` machinery plus the hidden `--intern-selftest` and `--intern-selftest-type-error` modes are embedded in the compiler under test. The self-compilation fixed point now includes code that exists only for tests, and a lone-argument invocation silently runs a self-test and exits 0 instead of producing the existing usage error. This is scope beyond "hash the intern table"; the probe belongs in a separate `.rb` fixture the test runs.

4. [MINOR] tests/bootstrap_selfhost_test.rs:2221 — Three separate tests (lines 2165, 2187, 2221) each spawn a fresh compiler process and re-run the *entire* `intern_selftest`, including the 1000-repeat loop, the 20,000-candidate collision search, and the 10 KB×10,000 append loop. The suite pays the full heavy self-test three times for overlapping data. Fix: run it once (shared result / one test asserting all keys) or split the modes.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 4
